          "turn_index": 2,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "And is it ever a sign of something worse?",
          "answer": "The referent is clear here: \"it\" is the heartburn you described most evenings. Heartburn can occasionally go with something more serious, so here is what the material I searched says.\n\n**Yes, it can sometimes be a sign of something more serious.** The most important example is heart trouble. The chest-pain guidance says heartburn and heart pain are not reliably told apart by how they feel. A history of reflux does not rule out a heart cause, and relief from antacids does not rule it out either (Emergency guidance, red-flag-chest-pain). Heart attacks can also show up as indigestion-like discomfort, especially in women, older adults and people with diabetes (red-flag-chest-pain).\n\n**Call emergency services now if you have:**\n- Chest pain, pressure or tightness, or discomfort that spreads to your arm, neck, jaw or back.\n- That discomfort with breathlessness, sweating, nausea, or when you exert yourself.\n- Sudden tearing chest or back pain, or chest pain with fainting (red-flag-chest-pain).\n- Sudden face drooping, arm weakness, or trouble speaking. Do not wait to see whether it passes (red-flag-stroke-symptoms).\n\n**Seek prompt medical review, the same day, if you have:**\n- Difficulty or pain when swallowing.\n- Vomiting blood, coffee-ground vomit, or black tarry stools (red-flag-gastrointestinal-bleeding; condition-gerd).\n- Unintentional weight loss.\n\nThe general reflux reference says these features need prompt assessment, and that ongoing symptoms may call for further testing, such as a camera test of the gullet (condition-gerd).\n\n**How urgently:** If any of the emergency features above apply, call emergency services now. If none apply, the material supports getting a clinician to look at heartburn that keeps coming back. The swallowing, bleeding and weight-loss features call for prompt review, not a routine wait.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.\n[sources: red-flag-chest-pain, red-flag-stroke-symptoms, red-flag-gastrointestinal-bleeding, condition-gerd]",
